 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "No wolf, shirt or blood drawn; Ya'qub: no plate. Their story (17) is framed once by As-Sa'di's «متعذرين بعذر كاذب», which stays on screen; the shirt by «زعموا». Geometric for «والله المستعان». Cut: «صبرا جميلا» (70:5) and passage echoes. STAGING v4: Both chapters: the family's tents in the desert at night (16: at the time of 'isha, the start of the night, Al-Muyassar), drawn without the crescent (moon: false), so no moon stands over the brothers and their father (the dream's echo, review 12a M3). Ya'qub (right) a blue drop labelled Ya'qub (no close-up, pan or glow), his sons three faceless men in plain robes (people, not the deniers' dark robes: they repent later). c1 (16-17): the brothers walk in to their father (16:1); the camera tilts up to the night sky for at night (16:3) and an hourglass plate for the late hour (As-Sa'di: later than their habit); nobody is shown weeping. They speak (17:1, 17:8, 17:12); their story is never acted: no racing, no belongings, no wolf; it stays framed by the gloss of a false excuse. c2 (18): the shirt and the blood are never drawn; the camera is on the brothers for what they brought (18:2), then Ya'qub answers (18:6) and shakes his head (18:8: he did not believe them, both tafsirs), so their claim is never shown as true; he speaks again (18:12, 18:18); a candle plate for beautiful patience (18:12-13) and geometric for Allah is the One sought for help (18:14-18). Cover: the brothers speaking to their father at night, no moon (title: the brothers' ruse). For the human reviewer: 3 figures = a group, not their number (the brothers are never counted; review 12a M1)."
